.policy "drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored" revision 1
.description "Put read-only and write-only options on a DRF serializer's explicitly declared field, not in its Meta; Meta options don't apply to declared fields."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. ModelSerializer applies Meta.read_only_fields and Meta.extra_kwargs only to the
// fields it builds from the model; a field the serializer declares (`username = serializers.CharField()`), itself or
// through a base serializer of the run in any module, ignores both, silently (DRF Serializers guide, two notes; DRF
// issues #3533, closed as intended, and #3460). A field listed read-only stays writable, so any client can set it
// (OWASP API3, mass assignment); `extra_kwargs = {"password": {"write_only": True}}` on a declared password leaves it
// in every response.
// It matches a ModelSerializer (or HyperlinkedModelSerializer) outside test code with a field x declared as a field
// call (a rest_framework field or a subclass, a nested serializer of the run, a `…Field`/`…Serializer` of another
// package), its own or the nearest run base serializer's that no class in between reassigns (`x = None` removes it),
// and whose Meta, its own or inherited (`class Meta(Base.Meta)`, or no Meta of its own), names x:
//   - in read_only_fields (a list, a tuple, `+`, `*splat`, `Other.Meta.read_only_fields`), unless the declared field
//     is read-only anyway: `read_only=True`, or a SerializerMethodField, ReadOnlyField, HiddenField,
//     HyperlinkedIdentityField, StringRelatedField or a subclass of one;
//   - as a key of extra_kwargs (a dict literal or `dict(...)`), unless every option of the entry is one the declared
//     call already passes with the same text (or `read_only: True` on a field read-only anyway, or `required: False`
//     on one with a `default=` or read-only: neither is required anyway), or the entry is empty. A field both lists
//     is reported for read_only_fields only.
// Once per serializer and field, at the place the fix starts from: the name in the Meta option when that name is
// written in the serializer's own body (its own Meta); else at the field's declaration when the serializer declares
// it; else (both inherited) at the class name, and only when no base serializer already has the same pair of name
// and declaration (that base is reported, not every subclass).
//   class UserSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
//       username = serializers.CharField(max_length=150)
//       full_name = serializers.SerializerMethodField()
//       class Meta:
//           model = User
//           fields = ["id", "username", "full_name"]
//           read_only_fields = ["username", "full_name"]   reported at "username"; full_name is read-only anyway
//   class SignupSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
//       password = serializers.CharField(write_only=True)
//       class Meta:
//           model = User
//           fields = ["username", "password"]
//           extra_kwargs = {"username": {"required": True}}  not reported: username is not declared
// Also left alone: a serializer whose own or a run base's `__init__` or `get_fields` reads the option by name
// (a mixin applying read_only_fields to the declared fields itself, as addons-server's version serializer does);
// for read_only_fields, a serializer that refuses all input (its own or a run base's `validate`,
// `to_internal_value` or `run_validation` raises unconditionally); plain Serializers; test code.
// Gaps: a field declared by two bases in a diamond takes the nearest along each path, not DRF's MRO; a project field
// class whose own __init__ forces read_only is reported; extra_kwargs built by a call other than dict(), a `**`
// splat or a comprehension is not read; a base serializer whose name the run resolves only under another import root
// (label-studio's `from core... import`) is not followed.

#include "lib/drf.rerail"

.violation DeclaredReadOnlyIgnored(at: node, ser: symbol, x: symbol) "`{ser}` declares `{x}`, so DRF ignores read_only_fields for it and clients can write it. Set read_only=True on the declared field, or drop `{x}` from read_only_fields if writes are intended."
DeclaredReadOnlyIgnored(at, s, x) :- dfm_at(c, x, "read_only_fields", at), def_name(c, s).

.violation DeclaredExtraKwargsIgnored(at: node, ser: symbol, x: symbol) "`{ser}` declares `{x}`, so DRF ignores its extra_kwargs entry. Pass these arguments to the declared field and drop the entry; if the field already behaves as intended, only drop the entry."
DeclaredExtraKwargsIgnored(at, s, x) :- dfm_at(c, x, "extra_kwargs", at), def_name(c, s).

// ---- declarations ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfm_decl(c, x, k): serializer c's field x is declared as call k: in c's body, else in the nearest run base
// serializer that declares it with no class between it and c assigning x.
.decl dfm_decl(c: node, x: symbol, k: node)
dfm_decl(c, x, k) :- drf_declared_own(c, x, k).
dfm_decl(c, x, k) :- drf_serializer(c), drf_ancestor(c, b), drf_declared_own(b, x, k), !drf_own_attr_name(c, x),
    !dfm_shadowed(c, b, x).
.decl dfm_shadowed(c: node, b: node, x: symbol)
dfm_shadowed(c, b, x) :- drf_ancestor(c, m), drf_ancestor(m, b), drf_declared_own(b, x, _), drf_own_attr_name(m, x).
// dfm_fieldish(k): call k builds a serializer field, so DRF collects it as a declared field: a rest_framework field
// or a subclass, a nested serializer of the run, or a `…Field`/`…Serializer` class from another package. A class of
// the run that derives from no DRF class (InvenTree's OptionalField, a placeholder its mixin swaps for a field) is
// not one.
.decl dfm_fieldish(k: node)
dfm_fieldish(k) :- drf_declared_own(_, _, k), drf_field_lib(k, _).
dfm_fieldish(k) :- drf_declared_own(_, _, k), drf_nested(k, _).
dfm_fieldish(k) :- drf_declared_own(_, _, k), call_name(k, t), (suffix("Field", t) ; suffix("Serializer", t)),
    !dfm_run_callee(k).
.decl dfm_run_callee(k: node)
dfm_run_callee(k) :- drf_declared_own(_, _, k), field(k, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q), class_def(_, q).
// dfm_ro(k): the declared field is read-only whatever Meta says.
.decl dfm_ro_kind(t: symbol)
dfm_ro_kind("SerializerMethodField"). dfm_ro_kind("ReadOnlyField"). dfm_ro_kind("HiddenField").
dfm_ro_kind("HyperlinkedIdentityField"). dfm_ro_kind("StringRelatedField").
.decl dfm_ro(k: node)
dfm_ro(k) :- drf_declared_own(_, _, k), drf_kw_true(k, "read_only").
dfm_ro(k) :- drf_declared_own(_, _, k), drf_field_kind(k, t), dfm_ro_kind(t).

// dfm_applied(c, o): serializer c, or a class of the run among its bases, has an `__init__` or `get_fields` that
// names option o (`self.Meta.read_only_fields`, `getattr(self.Meta, "read_only_fields", ())`): it applies the option
// itself.
.decl dfm_applied(c: node, o: symbol)
dfm_applied(c, o) :- drf_model_serializer(c), dfm_reads_opt(c, o).
dfm_applied(c, o) :- drf_model_serializer(c), drf_ancestor(c, b), dfm_reads_opt(b, o).
.decl dfm_reads_opt(b: node, o: symbol)
dfm_reads_opt(b, o) :- (m = "__init__" ; m = "get_fields"), drf_own_method(b, m, f), within(n, f),
    (attr_of(n, _, o) ; str(n, o)), (o = "read_only_fields" ; o = "extra_kwargs").
// A serializer that refuses all input (its own or a run base's `validate`, `to_internal_value` or `run_validation`
// raises as a statement of its body, as pretix's `raise TypeError("this serializer is readonly")`) writes no field:
// read_only_fields has nothing to protect.
dfm_applied(c, "read_only_fields") :- drf_model_serializer(c), dfm_refuses_input(c).
dfm_applied(c, "read_only_fields") :- drf_model_serializer(c), drf_ancestor(c, b), dfm_refuses_input(b).
.decl dfm_refuses_input(b: node)
dfm_refuses_input(b) :- (m = "validate" ; m = "to_internal_value" ; m = "run_validation"), drf_own_method(b, m, f),
    field(f, "body", fb), body_stmt(fb, s, _), kind(s, "raise_statement").

// ---- Meta values -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfm_ser(c): a ModelSerializer outside test code.
.decl dfm_ser(c: node)
dfm_ser(c) :- drf_model_serializer(c), docof(c, d), !dj_test_doc(d).
// dfm_elem(v, e, s): string literal e, of value s, is a name read_only_fields value v holds (drf_str_elem with the
// string's node).
.decl dfm_rof(v: node)
dfm_rof(v) :- dfm_ser(c), drf_meta_opt(c, "read_only_fields", v).
.decl dfm_elem(v: node, e: node, s: symbol)
dfm_elem(v, e, s) :- dfm_rof(v), dfm_elem_in(v, e, s).
.decl dfm_elem_in(v: node, e: node, s: symbol)
dfm_elem_in(v, e, s) :- unparen(v, e), str(e, s).
dfm_elem_in(v, e, s) :- unparen(v, u), kind(u, k), drf_seq(k), child(u, x, _), unparen(x, e), str(e, s).
dfm_elem_in(v, e, s) :- unparen(v, u), kind(u, "binary_operator"), op(u, "+"),
    (field(u, "left", x) ; field(u, "right", x)), dfm_elem_in(x, e, s).
dfm_elem_in(v, e, s) :- unparen(v, u), kind(u, k), drf_seq(k), child(u, sp, _), kind(sp, "list_splat"),
    child(sp, x, 0), dfm_elem_in(x, e, s).
dfm_elem_in(v, e, s) :- unparen(v, u), attr_of(u, o, k), attr_of(o, b, "Meta"), sym_of(b, bq), class_def(bc, bq),
    drf_meta_opt(bc, k, w), dfm_elem_in(w, e, s).

// dfm_ek(v, e, x, o): extra_kwargs value v has an entry for field x at node e (the key, or a dict() keyword's value)
// whose options are o.
.decl dfm_ekv(v: node)
dfm_ekv(v) :- dfm_ser(c), drf_meta_opt(c, "extra_kwargs", v).
.decl dfm_ek(v: node, e: node, x: symbol, o: node)
dfm_ek(v, e, x, o) :- dfm_ekv(v), unparen(v, d), kind(d, "dictionary"), child(d, p, _), kind(p, "pair"),
    field(p, "key", e), str(e, x), field(p, "value", pv), unparen(pv, o).
dfm_ek(v, o, x, o) :- dfm_ekv(v), unparen(v, d), kind(d, "call"), field(d, "function", f), sym_of(f, "builtins.dict"),
    drf_kw(d, x, pv), unparen(pv, o).
// dfm_opt(o, key, val): options dict o sets key to val: a dict literal or `dict(key=val)`.
.decl dfm_opt(o: node, key: symbol, val: node)
dfm_opt(o, key, val) :- dfm_ek(_, _, _, o), kind(o, "dictionary"), child(o, p, _), kind(p, "pair"),
    field(p, "key", kn), str(kn, key), field(p, "value", val).
dfm_opt(o, key, val) :- dfm_ek(_, _, _, o), kind(o, "call"), field(o, "function", f), sym_of(f, "builtins.dict"),
    drf_kw(o, key, val).
.decl dfm_lit(o: node)
dfm_lit(o) :- dfm_ek(_, _, _, o), kind(o, "dictionary").
dfm_lit(o) :- dfm_ek(_, _, _, o), kind(o, "call"), field(o, "function", f), sym_of(f, "builtins.dict").
// dfm_live(o, k): entry o says something declared call k does not: an option k does not pass with the same text, or
// options the rule cannot read.
.decl dfm_cand(o: node, k: node)
dfm_cand(o, k) :- dfm_ser(c), drf_meta_opt(c, "extra_kwargs", v), dfm_ek(v, _, x, o), dfm_decl(c, x, k).
.decl dfm_same(o: node, k: node, key: symbol)
dfm_same(o, k, key) :- dfm_cand(o, k), dfm_opt(o, key, val), drf_kw(k, key, kv), text(kv, t), text(val, t).
dfm_same(o, k, "read_only") :- dfm_cand(o, k), dfm_opt(o, "read_only", val), kind(val, "true"), dfm_ro(k).
// A field with a default (or a read-only one) is already not required: `required: False` asks nothing new.
dfm_same(o, k, "required") :- dfm_cand(o, k), dfm_opt(o, "required", val), kind(val, "false"),
    (drf_kw(k, "default", _) ; dfm_ro(k)).
.decl dfm_live(o: node, k: node)
dfm_live(o, k) :- dfm_cand(o, k), dfm_opt(o, key, _), !dfm_same(o, k, key).
dfm_live(o, k) :- dfm_cand(o, k), !dfm_lit(o).

// ---- hits and where they are reported ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfm_hit(c, x, opt, e, k): serializer c's Meta option opt names its declared field x (call k) at node e, uselessly.
.decl dfm_hit(c: node, x: symbol, opt: symbol, e: node, k: node)
dfm_hit(c, x, "read_only_fields", e, k) :- dfm_ser(c), drf_meta_opt(c, "read_only_fields", v), dfm_elem(v, e, x),
    dfm_decl(c, x, k), dfm_fieldish(k), !dfm_ro(k), !dfm_applied(c, "read_only_fields").
dfm_hit(c, x, "extra_kwargs", e, k) :- dfm_ser(c), drf_meta_opt(c, "extra_kwargs", v), dfm_ek(v, e, x, o),
    dfm_decl(c, x, k), dfm_fieldish(k), dfm_live(o, k), !dfm_applied(c, "extra_kwargs"), !dfm_rof_hit(c, x).
.decl dfm_rof_hit(c: node, x: symbol)
dfm_rof_hit(c, x) :- dfm_ser(c), drf_meta_opt(c, "read_only_fields", v), dfm_elem(v, _, x), dfm_decl(c, x, k),
    dfm_fieldish(k), !dfm_ro(k), !dfm_applied(c, "read_only_fields").
// A base serializer of c with the same pair is reported itself; c, inheriting both, is not.
.decl dfm_inherited(c: node, x: symbol, opt: symbol)
dfm_inherited(c, x, opt) :- dfm_hit(c, x, opt, e, k), drf_ancestor(c, b), dfm_hit(b, x, opt, e, k).
.decl dfm_at(c: node, x: symbol, opt: symbol, at: node)
dfm_at(c, x, opt, e) :- dfm_hit(c, x, opt, e, _), within(e, c).
dfm_at(c, x, opt, a) :- dfm_hit(c, x, opt, e, k), !within(e, c), drf_own_attr(c, x, v, a), unparen(v, k).
dfm_at(c, x, opt, n) :- dfm_hit(c, x, opt, e, _), !within(e, c), !drf_own_attr_name(c, x),
    !dfm_inherited(c, x, opt), field(c, "name", n).

// The cases, `cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/`, read as one repository: each line ending in
// `# caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "core/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/core/__init__.py"
    .fixture "core/fields.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/core/fields.py"
    .fixture "core/serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/core/serializers.py"
    .fixture "accounts/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/__init__.py"
    .fixture "accounts/models.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/models.py"
    .fixture "accounts/serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/serializers.py"
    .fixture "accounts/tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "accounts/tests/test_serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-declared-field-meta-ignored/accounts/tests/test_serializers.py"
    .expect _ at "core/serializers.py":22
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":25
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":47
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":60
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":73
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":92
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":100
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":105
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":166
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":192
.end
